  "id": "COMPOUND:30862 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "Robinin is implicated in the biological activity of SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular pathways, all of which converge on the compound MIP. The evidence suggests that Robinin directly targets MIP, which in turn acts as a target for multiple structurally diverse compounds, including Sophoradiol and a complex, cyclic ether compound. These targets are all ultimately linked to SMMC-7721, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of cellular processes through the interaction with these molecules. The presence of multiple distinct molecular structures as targets of MIP supports the idea that Robinin may influence SMMC-7721 through a broad, non-specific interaction, possibly involving receptor binding or enzyme inhibition. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Robinin and SMMC-7721, emphasizing the role of MIP as a central mediator in this interaction.",
